1 ADD

   Adds an account: a copy of the DEFAULT record with the fields the
   qualifiers give, and an identifier, the username, for its UIC.
   ADD/IDENTIFIER adds a rights identifier instead.

   Format

     ADD username [/qualifier...]

2 Parameters

 username

   1 to 12 letters, digits, dollar signs, and underscores.

2 Description

   DEFAULT's record has DISUSER set, so a new account can't log in until
   /FLAGS=NODISUSER clears it.  Without /UIC the account takes DEFAULT's,
   [200,200].  When another identifier has the UIC already, the account
   is added without one (%UAF-E-RDBADDERRU).

2 Qualifiers
/ACCOUNT

      /ACCOUNT=name

   The account name, up to 8 characters, for the accounting records.
   ADD makes it an identifier for the UIC's group, [g,*], when the group
   has none.

/ASTLM

      /ASTLM=n

   The most asynchronous system traps the process may have queued
   (AST limit).

/BIOLM

      /BIOLM=n

   The most buffered I/O requests the process may have outstanding.

/BYTLM

      /BYTLM=n

   The bytes the process's buffered I/O may use at once.

/CLI

      /CLI=name

   The command interpreter.  govax has only DCL; another name is kept,
   with a warning, and refused at login.

/CLITABLES

      /CLITABLES=name

   The command tables.  Kept and shown; govax has one set.

/CPUTIME

      /CPUTIME=delta

   The processor time a process may use, as a delta time
   ([d-]hh:mm:ss.cc), 0 for no limit.  Kept and shown; not enforced.

/DEFPRIVILEGES

      /DEFPRIVILEGES=(privilege[,...])

   The privileges a process of the account starts with, of those
   authorized.  A privilege's name sets it, NO and its name clears it, and
   ALL and NOALL set or clear every one; the others are left as they are.

/DEVICE

      /DEVICE=device

   The device of the home directory, SYS$LOGIN_DEVICE at login.

/DIOLM

      /DIOLM=n

   The most direct I/O requests the process may have outstanding.

/DIRECTORY

      /DIRECTORY=[directory]

   The home directory: SYS$LOGIN, SYS$SCRATCH, and the default directory
   at login.

/ENQLM

      /ENQLM=n

   The most locks the process may hold.

/FILLM

      /FILLM=n

   The most files the process may have open.

/FLAGS

      /FLAGS=([NO]flag[,...])

   The login flags, each named to set it or with NO to clear it:
   DISCTLY, DEFCLI, LOCKPWD, RESTRICTED, DISUSER, DISWELCOME,
   DISNEWMAIL, DISMAIL, GENPWD, PWD_EXPIRED, PWD2_EXPIRED, AUDIT,
   DISREPORT, DISRECONNECT, AUTOLOGIN, DISFORCE_PWD_CHANGE, CAPTIVE,
   DISIMAGE, DISPWDDIC, and DISPWDHIS.  Only DISUSER does anything in
   govax: it refuses the account's login.  The rest are kept and shown.

/JTQUOTA

      /JTQUOTA=n

   The bytes of the job's logical name table.

/LGICMD

      /LGICMD=filespec

   The account's login command procedure, run at login after
   SYS$SYLOGIN.  Without one, SYS$LOGIN:LOGIN.COM is run.

/MAXACCTJOBS

      /MAXACCTJOBS=n

   The most jobs the account's name may have at once.  Kept and shown.

/MAXDETACH

      /MAXDETACH=n

   The most detached processes the user may have.  Kept and shown.

/MAXJOBS

      /MAXJOBS=n

   The most jobs the user may have at once.  Kept and shown.

/OWNER

      /OWNER="name"

   The person the account belongs to, up to 31 characters.

/PASSWORD

      /[NO]PASSWORD=text

   The account's password, which govax keeps only as an Argon2id hash.
   Case doesn't matter.  /NOPASSWORD removes it.  An account with a
   password must give it at login (govax asks, or reads GOVAX_PASSWORD
   when standard input isn't a terminal); one without logs in asked for
   nothing.

/PBYTLM

      /PBYTLM=n

   The paged buffered I/O byte limit.  Kept and shown.

/PGFLQUOTA

      /PGFLQUOTA=n

   The pages of the page file the job may use.

/PRCLM

      /PRCLM=n

   The most subprocesses the process may have at once.

/PRIORITY

      /PRIORITY=n

   The base priority, 0 to 31.

/PRIVILEGES

      /PRIVILEGES=(privilege[,...])

   The privileges the account is authorized to hold.  A privilege's name
   sets it, NO and its name clears it, and ALL and NOALL set or clear
   every one; the others are left as they are.

/QUEPRIO

      /QUEPRIO=n

   The priority of the user's jobs in queues.  Kept and shown.

/SHRFILLM

      /SHRFILLM=n

   The most shared files the process may have open.  Kept and shown.

/TQELM

      /TQELM=n

   The most timer requests the process may have queued.

/UIC

      /UIC=[group,member]

   The user identification code, both numbers octal: the group 1 to
   37776, the member 1 to 177776.  Groups up to MAXSYSGROUP (octal 10) are
   system groups.

/WSDEFAULT

      /WSDEFAULT=n

   The working set's default size, in pages.

/WSEXTENT

      /WSEXTENT=n

   The most pages the working set may grow to.

/WSQUOTA

      /WSQUOTA=n

   The pages of working set the process is guaranteed.

/IDENTIFIER

      ADD/IDENTIFIER name [/VALUE=IDENTIFIER=n | /VALUE=UIC=[g,m]] [/ATTRIBUTES=(attribute[,...])]

   Adds a rights identifier, not an account.  Its value is the next free
   general identifier (%X80010000 and up), or /VALUE=IDENTIFIER=n (65536
   to 268435455), or /VALUE=UIC=[g,m] for a UIC identifier.  The
   attributes are RESOURCE, DYNAMIC, NOACCESS, SUBSYSTEM, IMPERSONATE,
   and HOLDER_HIDDEN.

/ATTRIBUTES

      /ATTRIBUTES=(attribute[,...])

   With /IDENTIFIER: the new identifier's attributes.

/VALUE

      /VALUE=IDENTIFIER=n or /VALUE=UIC=[g,m]

   With /IDENTIFIER: the new identifier's value, in place of the next
   free general one.

2 Examples

   1.UAF> ADD SMITH/UIC=[200,1]/OWNER="JOHN SMITH"/FLAGS=NODISUSER -
        /DEVICE=DUA1:/DIRECTORY=[SMITH]/PASSWORD=SECRET

     Adds SMITH, who logs in to DUA1:[SMITH].

   2.UAF> ADD/IDENTIFIER PROJX

     Adds the identifier PROJX, with the next general value.

1 COPY

   Adds an account that is a copy of another, with the fields the
   qualifiers give.

   Format

     COPY old-username new-username [/qualifier...]

2 Parameters

 old-username

   The account to copy.

 new-username

   The new account's username.

2 Description

   The copy has no password unless /PASSWORD gives one (%UAF-W-DEFPWD),
   and holds no identifiers.  Copied with the same UIC, it is
   %UAF-W-SAMEUIC.

