1 EXIT

   Ends an AUTHORIZE session, saying whether the accounts and the rights
   database changed.  Ctrl/Z does the same.

   Format

     EXIT

1 GRANT

   GRANT/IDENTIFIER lets an account's UIC hold a rights identifier.  Every
   account with the UIC holds it, and has it among its rights at login.

   Format

     GRANT/IDENTIFIER identifier username [/ATTRIBUTES=(attribute[,...])]

2 Parameters

 identifier

   The identifier to grant.

 username

   The account, by its UIC identifier's name.

2 Qualifiers
/IDENTIFIER

   Required: GRANT has only this form.

/ATTRIBUTES

      /ATTRIBUTES=(attribute[,...])

   The holder's attributes, only those the identifier has.

1 HELP

   Shows AUTHORIZE's help, from SYS$HELP:UAFHELP.HLB.

   Format

     HELP [topic [subtopic...]]

2 Description

   With no topic it lists the commands and asks for one.  At each
   prompt, a topic shows it, ? shows the list again, and Return goes up a
   level, back to the UAF> prompt at the top.

1 LIST

   Writes SHOW's report of accounts into SYSUAF.LIS in the default
   directory: every account, a line each, by default.  LIST/IDENTIFIER and
   LIST/RIGHTS write RIGHTSLIST.LIS.

   Format

     LIST [username] [/BRIEF | /FULL]

2 Parameters

 username

   The accounts to list; % and * match several.  Every one when left out.

2 Qualifiers
/BRIEF

   A line for each account, the default.

/FULL

   Each account's whole record, with the identifiers it holds.

/IDENTIFIER

      LIST/IDENTIFIER name

   The identifier, with its holders, into RIGHTSLIST.LIS.  A name is
   required (%UAF-I-NOIDNAME without one).

/VALUE

      /VALUE=IDENTIFIER=n or /VALUE=UIC=[g,m]

   With /IDENTIFIER: the identifier to list, by its value.

/RIGHTS

      LIST/RIGHTS username

   The identifiers the account's UIC holds, into RIGHTSLIST.LIS.

1 MODIFY

   Changes accounts: the fields the qualifiers give, the rest left alone.
   MODIFY/IDENTIFIER changes a rights identifier instead.

   Format

     MODIFY username [/qualifier...]

2 Parameters

 username

   The accounts to change; % and * match several, each changed.

2 Description

   A changed /UIC changes the account's UIC identifier too.

2 Qualifiers
/ACCOUNT

      /ACCOUNT=name

   The account name, up to 8 characters, for the accounting records.
   ADD makes it an identifier for the UIC's group, [g,*], when the group
   has none.

/ASTLM

      /ASTLM=n

   The most asynchronous system traps the process may have queued
   (AST limit).

/BIOLM

      /BIOLM=n

   The most buffered I/O requests the process may have outstanding.

/BYTLM

      /BYTLM=n

   The bytes the process's buffered I/O may use at once.

/CLI

      /CLI=name

   The command interpreter.  govax has only DCL; another name is kept,
   with a warning, and refused at login.

/CLITABLES

      /CLITABLES=name

   The command tables.  Kept and shown; govax has one set.

/CPUTIME

      /CPUTIME=delta

   The processor time a process may use, as a delta time
   ([d-]hh:mm:ss.cc), 0 for no limit.  Kept and shown; not enforced.

