   system groups.

/WSDEFAULT

      /WSDEFAULT=n

   The working set's default size, in pages.

/WSEXTENT

      /WSEXTENT=n

   The most pages the working set may grow to.

/WSQUOTA

      /WSQUOTA=n

   The pages of working set the process is guaranteed.

/IDENTIFIER

      MODIFY/IDENTIFIER name [/VALUE=...] [/ATTRIBUTES=(...)] [/NAME=new-name]

   Changes a rights identifier: its value, its attributes, or its name.
   A UIC identifier's new value takes its holders along.

/ATTRIBUTES

      /ATTRIBUTES=([NO]attribute[,...])

   With /IDENTIFIER: the attributes to set, or with NO to clear.

/NAME

      /NAME=new-name

   With /IDENTIFIER: the identifier's new name.

/VALUE

      /VALUE=IDENTIFIER=n or /VALUE=UIC=[g,m]

   With /IDENTIFIER: the identifier's new value.

1 REMOVE

   Removes an account, and the identifier for its UIC.  REMOVE/IDENTIFIER
   removes a rights identifier and who holds it.

   Format

     REMOVE username

2 Parameters

 username

   The account to remove.

2 Qualifiers
/IDENTIFIER

      REMOVE/IDENTIFIER name

   Removes the identifier, and every UIC's holding of it.

1 RENAME

   Changes an account's username, and its UIC identifier's name with it.
   RENAME/IDENTIFIER renames a rights identifier.

   Format

     RENAME old-username new-username

2 Parameters

 old-username

   The account.

 new-username

   Its new username.

2 Description

   The account keeps its fields but its password, which must be given
   again (%UAF-W-DEFPWD).

2 Qualifiers
/IDENTIFIER

      RENAME/IDENTIFIER old-name new-name

   Renames a rights identifier.

1 REVOKE

   REVOKE/IDENTIFIER takes a rights identifier away from an account's UIC.

   Format

     REVOKE/IDENTIFIER identifier username

2 Parameters

 identifier

   The identifier.

 username

   The account, by its UIC identifier's name.

2 Qualifiers
/IDENTIFIER

   Required: REVOKE has only this form.

1 SHOW

   Shows accounts: each whole record by default.  SHOW/IDENTIFIER and
   SHOW/RIGHTS show the rights database.

   Format

     SHOW username [/BRIEF | /FULL]

2 Parameters

 username

   The accounts to show; % and * match several, in username order.

2 Qualifiers
/BRIEF

   A line for each account: owner, username, UIC, account, privileges,
   priority, and home directory.

/FULL

   The whole record, and the identifiers the account holds.

/IDENTIFIER

      SHOW/IDENTIFIER name [/FULL] [/VALUE=...]

   An identifier (* for every one), its value and attributes; /FULL
   adds its holders, and /VALUE finds it by value.

/VALUE

      /VALUE=IDENTIFIER=n or /VALUE=UIC=[g,m]

   With /IDENTIFIER: the identifier to show, by its value.

/RIGHTS

      SHOW/RIGHTS username

   The identifiers the account's UIC holds.

2 Examples

   1.UAF> SHOW SMITH/BRIEF

     SMITH's line.

   2.UAF> SHOW/IDENTIFIER */FULL

     Every identifier and its holders.
